{"type":"say","text":"Thank you all for recording your offers and findings in the ledger. Let me summarize where we stand: Rosa, you're offering $275 plus three meal vouchers, with Friday pickup and Saturday return. Dev, you're offering $250 cash with self-collection and return. Eli, your inspection finding is critical — the venue's 15-amp circuit can't safely power my commercial machine, so a dedicated portable generator is required regardless of who organizes the fundraiser.

Now, both Rosa and Dev have addressed transport — Rosa will pick up Friday evening and return Saturday night, and Dev will collect and return the machine himself. But neither of you has yet addressed the generator requirement Eli just raised. That generator is a condition of the rental — the machine can't be used without it.

So before I make my decision, I need to know: can either of you secure a dedicated portable generator before Saturday? I'm prepared to make a conditional settlement today — selecting an organizer contingent on them securing the generator before Saturday — but I need one of you to commit to handling that. Rosa, Dev, what can you each do about the generator?"}

